## Test and quality contract

Every behavior change requires an explicit test impact assessment. Cover normal, invalid, boundary, failure, retry, timeout, concurrency and idempotency behavior where applicable. Use integration or E2E tests when the risk crosses a process, storage, network, browser or deployment boundary. Do not claim 100% correctness from line coverage alone.

Required checks for this repository: `<verified checks>`
Coverage or mutation thresholds, if enforced: `<verified thresholds>`

## Change safety

- Preserve unrelated worktree changes.
- Do not reset, delete, overwrite or migrate data without explicit scope and a recoverable plan.
- Do not change package scripts, public names or configuration semantics unless the task requires it.
- Separate local verification from deployed verification.
- Record unresolved risks instead of silently assuming them away.

## Delivery acceptance

Before reporting completion, provide:

1. files changed and why;
2. implementation summary;
3. checks actually run and their results;
4. acceptance criteria status;
5. remaining risks or unverified boundaries.
